{"id":"int-c196603068c649696fb282b725997457","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-17T15:03:47.152075252Z","actor":"Will Winder","issue_id":"muscle-mass-chart-99e","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed: redefined percentOfPeak as % of the sedentary reference peak (PRD §5.2 updated), removed the Math.min(100,...) clamp in computeCurve.js, raised strengthTraining bonus targets so trained scenarios clear the disability threshold at old age, and widened the chart's Y axis to 140."}}
{"id":"int-fe4ea8999e12526b4875ff736c879fe8","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-17T15:17:58.77607284Z","actor":"Will Winder","issue_id":"muscle-mass-chart-8bx","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Added a per-activity decline-retention factor (ACTIVITY_TARGET_RETENTION in computeCurve.js) alongside the existing peak bonus: post-peak years now apply only a fraction of the sedentary curve's year-over-year decline for trained scenarios, producing a plateau and a gap that widens with age instead of a constant offset. Verified numerically against the sedentary baseline and all 4 presets."}}
